  "editorReview": {
    "text": "This narrative history of sugar's global impact succeeds when it grounds its bold 'Sweetness Stack' concept in vivid material details—like the conical clay molds of early refining or the immobilized enzymes in a modern Iowa plant. However, the middle chapters too often lose their storyteller's voice, slipping into a passive, textbook-like register that severs the narrative seams and flattens the drama. While the concluding analysis on the 'cost distance' of empire regains its moral urgency, the journey there can feel uneven.",
